# Organised by intent rather than by tool, following tiny-model-lab's
# .gitignore. The principle there is "provenance is committed, bytes are not".
# Here the fixture is provenance, not bytes: it is the oracle the port is
# measured against, so it is tracked on purpose.

# Build output
dist
dist-ssr
*.local

# Node
node_modules
logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
lerna-debug.log*

# Python — tools/ only. Nothing under src/ imports any of it, and none of it
# is bundled. music21 is a dev-time oracle, not a dependency of the page.
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# The fixture IS tracked. It is what test/parity.test.ts compares against, and
# a repo that regenerates its own oracle on demand has no oracle.
!fixtures/*.json

# Harness output, if a contract ever lands in experiments/. Same split as
# tiny-model-lab: manifests and ledgers are the decision trail and are kept;
# the artifacts they describe are not.
#
# `champion/*` and not `champion/`. With the trailing slash git excludes the
# directory and never descends into it, so no `!` below can rescue anything
# inside -- which quietly loses champion.json, the card naming which run is
# current and what it scored. In a fresh clone harness's _load_champion()
# would then find nothing, and the *next* promotion's strict-improvement
# check would not run at all. A gitignore line would have disabled the guard
# that promote.py exists to provide.
#
# The card is provenance, so it is kept. The promoted artifact is not kept
# yet, because nothing has been promoted and where it should live is an open
# decision: a table small enough for the page to bundle is arguably source
# rather than a checkpoint, which would invert this file's usual rule the way
# fixtures/ does above. Decide that when there is something to promote, and
# add the `!` line then rather than pre-committing to an answer here.
runs/*/artifacts/
champion/*
!champion/champion.json
!runs/*/manifest.json
!runs/LEDGER.md

# The blank contract `harness init` drops in experiments/. Not tracked, on the
# same reasoning that keeps fixtures/ tracked, run backwards: the fixture is an
# oracle and regenerating it on demand would leave this repo without one, while
# this is a form that `init` rewrites on demand and that belongs to
# tiny-model-lab. A vendored copy would drift from the original and say nothing
# the original does not. It is also not a contract -- the guard's glob is
# `*.yaml` and this is not one, which is the whole point of the name
# (tiny-model-lab#21).
experiments/*.yaml.template

# Exports of .claude/, once there is a .claude/ to export. Committing copies
# would mean two divergent versions of the same hook in one repo.
.agents/
.codex/

# Editor and OS
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea
.DS_Store
*.suo
*.ntvs*
*.njsproj
*.sln
*.sw?
